# ---- The per-class rename table (the irreducible tail) --------------------
# The packages below do NOT map uniformly: android.support.v4.app splits into
# androidx.fragment.app vs androidx.core.app; v7.widget splits into
# recyclerview.widget vs appcompat.widget; support.test fans out per class.
# The ground truth here is jetifier's finite per-class mapping — a TABLE.
#
# GAP-3 (REVISED after discussion): these rows are NOT a systematic edit in
# summarize's sense. Anti-unifying them yields the vacuous `import _H0 ->
# import _H1`; the commonality (jetifier's map, the migration intent) is
# domain knowledge outside the diff. A "table rule" would be memorization,
# not inference — no compression, no prediction — so support-1 rows are
# CORRECTLY residuals under §5.5, and support>=2 rows are already honest
# concrete rules. What's genuinely improvable is presentational: residual
# GROUPING by hunk shape ("19 residual sites share the form `- import ...` /
# `+ import ...`"), which aids review without claiming rule-hood. A
# disjunction construct remains defensible only on the AUTHORING side
# (writing a jetifier-style patch for `apply`, cf. Coccinelle's ( A | B )),
# which is a transforms feature, not a summarize gap.
#
#  n  old import                                        new import
#  4  android.support.v4.content.ContextCompat          androidx.core.content.ContextCompat
#  4  android.support.v7.widget.LinearLayoutManager     androidx.recyclerview.widget.LinearLayoutManager
#  3  android.support.v7.widget.RecyclerView            androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView
#  3  android.support.v4.app.Fragment                   androidx.fragment.app.Fragment
#  2  android.support.v7.app.AlertDialog                androidx.appcompat.app.AlertDialog
