#
# GAP-2: rows like arch.persistence.db.framework.* and room.migration.* are
# package-PREFIX renames with a multi-segment tail. `import
# android.arch.persistence.room.TAIL` with TAIL spanning `migration.Migration`
# needs a sequence-shaped metavar inside a dotted path; `single` cannot span
# segments, and sequence metavars only match sibling lists today.

# ---- Semi-systematic ride-alongs (support 2, rule-or-residual borderline) --
# GAP-5 (proposer, known): the InstantTaskExecutorRule additions are PURE
# INSERTIONS — a new @get:Rule property + org.junit.Rule import added to two
# test classes (AppDatabaseTest, NetworkLeaderboardDaoTest), required by the
# androidx test runner. As a pattern this needs a positional anchor
# ("first member of the class body"), which context lines cannot express
# when the surrounding members differ — and the anchored proposer excludes
# pure insertions by design. Residual today; arguably rule-worthy.
#
# Also support-2: the PrivacyPractices test refactor (TermsOfService ->
# Summary.UNKNOWN import + argument reshuffle) — left as residual here
# because the two sites' code edits differ in shape.

# ---- Residuals (the ride-alongs a reviewer should actually read) ----------
# Listed as file -> what happened; full diffs omitted in this hand-written
# document (baseline.summary carries the exact hunks).
#
# FileUtilities.kt                 -> unused loadLines() DELETED (pure ride-along)
# FileChooserIntentBuilderTest.kt  -> clipData -> clipData?.  (behaviour: nullability)
# UserAgentProviderTest.kt         -> regex-escaping edits in two test strings
# QueryUrlConverterTest.kt         -> encodedQuery null-handling rework (assertNotNull + !!),
#                                     Assert.* wildcard import swap
# HttpsBloomFilterSpecDaoTest.kt   -> specification!! -> specification (smart-cast cleanup)
# ApiRequestInterceptorTest.kt     -> getContext() -> getInstrumentation().context — the ONE
#                                     site keeping instrumentation-context semantics (cf. A3)
# UnsentForgetAllPixelStoreSharedPreferencesTest.kt -> fully-qualified androidx
#                                     InstrumentationRegistry usage (import dropped)
# SingleLiveEvent.kt               -> Observer<T> -> Observer<in T> (variance, androidx API)
# TabSwitcherAdapter.kt            -> RecyclerView.ViewHolder(root) -> ViewHolder(root) + import
# TestExtensions.kt                -> @UiThread annotation + import added
# TestRunner.kt                    -> @Suppress("unused") added
# AppDatabaseTest.kt, NetworkLeaderboardDaoTest.kt -> InstantTaskExecutorRule @get:Rule
#                                     insertion (GAP-5); NetworkLeaderboardDaoTest also gains
#                                     .allowMainThreadQueries()
# TrackerDetectorTest.kt           -> wildcard import expanded to 3 explicit; const removed
# TrackerDetectorListTest.kt       -> unused imports dropped (PrevalenceStore, Mock)
# PredefinedGradeTest.kt           -> unused imports dropped; Input class reformat
# PrivacyPracticesTest.kt          -> private val added; mock setup reformat; imports dropped
# PrivacyDashboardViewModelTest.kt, PrivacyPracticesViewModelTest.kt ->
#                                     TermsOfService -> PrivacyPractices.Summary refactor
# OnboardingViewModelTest.kt       -> unused VariantManager mock + import removed
# TabDataRepositoryTest.kt         -> unused TermsOfServiceStore import removed
# PrevalenceRawStoreTest.kt        -> unused org.junit.Assert import removed
# SiteMonitorTest.kt, TrackerDataDaoTest.kt, BloomFilterTest.kt ->
#                                     private/val visibility-style tweaks
# WebViewDataManagerTest.kt        -> trailing-lambda style: (mockCookieManager, {}) -> (mockCookieManager) {}
# WebViewLongPressHandlerTest.kt, ClearPersonalDataActionTest.kt, TabsDaoTest.kt,
# AppDatabaseTest.kt               -> multi-line call re-wrapping (formatting-only;
#                                     should vanish under --ignore-formatting)
#
# GAP-6 (residual noise, not expressiveness): after-side import blocks are
# re-SORTED (androidx sorts differently than android.arch/android.support).
# Rules rewrite lines in place, so pure reorder moves leak into residuals
# even when every line is rule-explained. An order-insensitive treatment of
# import blocks (normalize order before residual computation, or declare
# import lists unordered regions) would eliminate this class of noise.
